  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img height=\"71\" src=\"assets\\st0187_f56145481971.png\" width=\"567\" /><br /><br />The final product is an isocyanide as the <math><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></math> bond has covalent nature, due to which <math><mi>C</mi></math> is unavailable for bond. Hence, N bonds with the benzylic carbon leading to formation of isocyanide.</p>"
